# Exclusions for the `make chaos-container` build context. Not the repo-root
# .dockerignore, which excludes test/ and scripts/ and so cannot serve an image
# that needs test/chaos/**; the Makefile stages a filtered copy of the repo with
# these patterns and places this file at the staged root (see the comment above
# the `test-isolation` target, which this mirrors).
#
# Patterns follow rsync --exclude-from syntax (used by the Makefile target), not
# Docker's own .dockerignore dialect. Anchored (leading /) entries match only at
# the repo root; web/dist/ must stay, since //go:embed dist (web/embed.go) needs
# its tracked placeholder to compile.
.git/
web/node_modules/
bin/
/runs/
.superpowers/
.venv-docs/
.venv/
.venv-oracle/
__pycache__/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
coverage/
/clients/python/dist/
/clients/submitter/dist/
